    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just sadness. it's like... looking at the scale of everything. i look at the skyscrapers and the millions of lights, and i realize i'm just a tiny, mathematical error in the system. if i was gone, the math of this city stays exactly the same. there's no hole left behind. it feels more like a fact than a feeling.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
